<script>
 import AppIcon from './AppIcon.svelte';
 import {tick,createEventDispatcher} from 'svelte';
 export let open=false;
 const dispatch=createEventDispatcher();let dialog,priorFocus;
 $:if(dialog&&open&&!dialog.open){priorFocus=document.activeElement;dialog.showModal();tick().then(()=>dialog.querySelector('button')?.focus());}
 $:if(dialog&&!open&&dialog.open){dialog.close();(priorFocus?.isConnected && priorFocus.getClientRects().length ? priorFocus : document.querySelector('[data-help-trigger]')?.getClientRects().length ? document.querySelector('[data-help-trigger]') : document.querySelector('[data-settings-trigger]'))?.focus({preventScroll:true});}
</script>
<dialog bind:this={dialog} aria-label="Help and keyboard shortcuts" on:cancel|preventDefault={()=>open=false}>
 <header><h2 class="dw-with-icon"><AppIcon name="help"/>Help</h2><button class="dw-btn-secondary" on:click={()=>open=false}><AppIcon name="close" size={16}/>Close Help</button></header>

 <p class="intro dw-muted">Choose a task for steps, recovery options, and shortcuts.</p>
 <details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="search"/><span>Find something you said</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Search entries by words, tags, title, or filename. Search spans the library. Narrow it with the date rail, Starred, MayDos, or Filters. The result summary names the scope; Clear filters restores it. Words search works without a model connection.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="transcript"/><span>Read and listen without losing your place</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Select an entry to open the reader beside the list. Previous and Next follow your current results. On a small screen, Back to entries returns to your list position. Transcript shows cleaned speech when available; Original keeps the raw transcription.</p><p>Select passage text to copy it. The time button starts audio at that passage. Copy and a selection checkbox appear when a passage is focused or hovered; both stay visible on touch screens. Check a passage to reveal the other checkboxes, then Copy selected joins checked passages in transcript order. Select all and Clear selection are in that toolbar; More → Select passages also starts selection. Copy transcript copies the full entry. Playback speed, Follow and Find are reader controls. Audio unavailable does not prevent reading.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="mic"/><span>Capture a recording</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Record asks for microphone access only when you start. Stop retains a draft; Save acknowledges the saved audio before processing. Retry keeps the same draft after an upload failure. Import accepts audio files without microphone access. Activity shows saved work, waiting for sync writes, progress, and retryable failures.</p><p>A blocked browser microphone needs a secure browser context and permission. Import remains available. Do not change network exposure just to enable recording.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="maydos"/><span>Decide whether an action is worth doing</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>MayDos are possible actions, not commitments. New suggestions start as Suggested. Mark one Selected when you choose it, Done after completion, or Dismissed when it does not fit. Changes offer a short Undo. Source reveals the supporting transcript; a timestamp plays it when available.</p><p>Use MayDos and status filters to find entries with actions. Older entries can be extracted in a scoped batch, stopped after the current entry, resumed, or retried only for failures.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="folder"/><span>Organize or recover an entry</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Reader More contains Assign recording date and Move to Trash. Organization previews both entries on conflict. Keep both is the default; replacement preserves the existing entry in Trash. Unfiled and Holding entries remain readable.</p><p>Move to Trash waits for the server acknowledgment, then offers eight-second Undo. Afterward, Settings → Data and maintenance → Trash can restore it. Restore keeps both when a destination exists. Permanent deletion requires naming and confirming the saved audio and transcript.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="waveform"/><span>Improve a difficult recording</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Reader More → Improve audio & retranscribe prepares a preview from the original recording when available. Choose Quiet speech, Uneven volume, Background noise or Unfiltered original, then listen before creating a new transcript. Large-v3 prioritizes quality; turbo is the faster option. Compare the current and candidate transcripts and choose which to keep. Your originals, tags, stars and MayDo decisions stay saved. Reopen this action for progress or Undo before further transcript changes. Choose Create readable after acceptance to restore punctuation and regular paragraphs. Check transcript reviews one flagged passage at a time, with bounded playback and alternate text when available.</p>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="activity"/><span>Fix processing or search</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><p>Activity shows the failed stage. Cleanup problems leave Original available; configure the host/model in the loaded configuration file, restart, then retry cleanup. Settings shows effective folders, runtimes, destinations, and diagnostics. A words-index rebuild changes only the derived cache.</p><button class="dw-btn-secondary" on:click={()=>{open=false;dispatch('settings');}}><AppIcon name="settings" size={16}/>Open Settings and recovery</button>
 </div></details>
<details class="help-topic dw-disclosure"><summary><AppIcon name="keyboard"/><span>Keyboard shortcuts</span></summary><div class="topic-body"><dl><dt>/</dt><dd>Focus library search outside text fields</dd><dt>?</dt><dd>Open this Help outside text fields</dd><dt>Enter</dt><dd>Open a focused entry</dd><dt>Escape</dt><dd>Close the current dialog or the reader's open More / Find control</dd><dt>Tab / Shift+Tab</dt><dd>Move between controls; dialogs keep focus inside</dd><dt>Space</dt><dd>Activate focused playback control</dd></dl></div></details>
</dialog>
<style>
  dialog{position:fixed;inset:0 0 0 auto;margin:0;width:min(560px,100vw);max-width:100vw;height:100dvh;max-height:100dvh;padding:0 20px 20px;background:var(--dw-surface);color:var(--dw-text);border:0;border-left:1px solid var(--dw-border);overflow:auto;}dialog::backdrop{background:#0009;}
  header{position:sticky;top:0;background:var(--dw-surface);padding:16px 0;z-index:2;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--dw-border);}h2{font-size:20px;}
  .intro{margin:16px 0;}.help-topic{border-top:1px solid var(--dw-border);}.help-topic summary{padding:14px 0;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.5;}.help-topic[open] summary{color:var(--dw-accent-bright);}
  .topic-body{padding:0 0 16px;}p{overflow-wrap:anywhere;line-height:1.65;font-size:14px;margin:10px 0;}button{min-height:44px;}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:10px 16px;font-size:14px;}dt{font-weight:600;color:var(--dw-accent-bright);}dd{line-height:1.5;}
  @media(max-width:400px){dialog{padding:0 16px 16px;}dl{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px;}dd{margin-bottom:8px;}}
</style>
